flowchart TB
  accTitle: LIDA competition and broadcast cycle
  accDescr: Specialized codelets process available information and contribute to related coalitions. Coalitions compete for limited global workspace access. A winning coalition is broadcast to memory, action selection, and learning processes. Downstream activity and learning can influence later cycles. The diagram shows a mechanism pattern and does not prescribe a numeric competition formula.
  subgraph C[Specialized processing]
    C1[Codelet A]
    C2[Codelet B]
    C3[Codelet C]
    C4[Codelet D]
  end
  C1 --> K[Related codelet coalition]
  C2 --> K
  C3 --> K2[Alternative coalition]
  C4 --> K2
  K --> X[Competition for limited workspace]
  K2 --> X
  X -->|winner| W[Global workspace]
  X -->|not admitted| H[Other candidates remain outside]
  W --> B[Broadcast selected content]
  B --> M[Memory]
  B --> A[Action selection]
  B --> L[Learning]
  M --> N[Later cycle]
  A --> N
  L --> N
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef process fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef output fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef caution fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#F39C12,color:#1C1C1E
  class C1,C2,C3,C4 source
  class K,K2,X,W,B process
  class M,A,L,N output
  class H caution
